EBS vs EFS vs S3

--> you can use s3 to store and retrieve any amount of data at any time, 
from anywhere on the web.
--> S3 is a object based storage.
--> S3 is a non bootable storage. you cannot install OS on S3.
--> S3 provides high avaialbility and durability.
--> durability is 99.999999999% (11 9's) and availability is 99.99% (4 9's).
--> s3 has distributed architecture, where objcets are stored in multiple locations
in a region. (stored in min 3 location within a region)

--> in s3 data stored in a bucket.
--> bucket is a flat container for objects.
--> can not create nested buckets.(bucket inside a bucket)
--> s3 is region specific.
-->  min and max capacity of s3 object is 0 byte to 50TB.
--> you can have upto 100 buckets per account by default. (can be increased by request)


